From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:33:31 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] cellPad: a second port for player 2, by the number of local
 players

ENHANCEMENT: on a PS3 each player has a controller. On a PC one player
often has the keyboard and mouse and the other a pad, or two people have a
pad each and the keyboard sits next to the first one.

Symptom (Killzone HD): the Multiplayer screen's "Two Player" stays greyed
out with the default controllers setting (merged: every pad on port 0), and
with one pad in either setting, because the game enables it only while
port 1 reads connected. With two pads and controllers=separate it worked,
but the mouse is applied on port 0 only through the title's hook, and a
player on the keyboard had no way to play with one pad.

Fix: the SDL backend reads each controller into its slot (the remembered
order the hot-plug code keeps), and pad_assign.h turns the slots into
ports from the number of local players, which the title sets with
pad_set_players (default 1), and the merged/separate choice:

- 1 player: as before (merged: every pad on port 0; separate: slot n on
  port n). Port 1 also reads connected whenever a pad is there, with
  neutral data (nothing pressed, sticks centred) when no pad feeds it.
- 2 players, 1 pad: the keyboard and mouse are player 1 (port 0), the pad
  is player 2 (port 1).
- 2 players, 2 or more pads: the first pad and the keyboard and mouse are
  player 1, the second pad player 2, the others none.

Which ports read connected does not depend on the number of players, so
the switch never looks like a controller coming or going. The keyboard and
mouse stay on port 0. Rumble for a port goes to the controllers that feed
it: player 1 on the keyboard no longer shakes player 2's pad, and merged
still rumbles every pad. The host test tools/tests/test_pad_assign.sh runs
pad_assign.h.
